1. Introduction

FMEDA (Failure Modes, Effects, and Diagnostic Analysis) is the quantitative core of ISO 26262 hardware evaluation. It analyzes component failure rates, diagnostic coverage (DC), and failure mode distributions to calculate three key metrics:

Metric ASIL D Target Purpose
SPFM (Single-Point Fault Metric) ≥ 99% Measures avoidance of single-point failures
LFM (Latent Fault Metric) ≥ 90% Measures avoidance of latent faults
PMHF (Probabilistic Metric for Hardware Failure) ≤ 10 FIT Random hardware failure probability per hour

This FMEDA demonstrates that ST-T1024's deterministic architecture inherently achieves these targets — not through complex safety mechanisms bolted on afterward, but through structural properties designed in from the start.

