5. Key Observations

5.1 Why ST-T1024 Exceeds ASIL D Targets

Structural Property Safety Benefit FMEDA Impact
75% ROM (immutable) Eliminates software corruption risks DC = 99.9% for memory faults
FSM-enforced AET (680 ns) Eliminates timing variability Converts WCET (statistical) → AET (deterministic)
Ternary logic (no multipliers) Reduces arithmetic fault surface Lower FIT for compute units
Power gating (99.9%) Zero leakage → lower thermal stress Extends component lifetime
TLA+ formal proof State invariants mathematically verified Eliminates illegal state transitions
Domain tiling Faults isolated to one tile Prevents fault propagation

5.2 Sources of Conservative Estimates

· Failure rates drawn from SN 29500 and IEC 62380 standards
· Diagnostic coverage values are conservative (99% vs. potential 99.9%)
· Temperature derating (−40°C to 125°C) not yet applied (would increase FIT)
· AEC-Q100 qualification would reduce baseline FIT further

